  <div class="tiles">
    <div><span class="k">L1 charm tag: c efficiency at 10% light mistag</span><span class="v">16% &rarr; 29% &rarr; 34%</span><span class="s">pixels nearly double it: NN &rarr; + pixel hits &rarr; + recalibrated displacement and a charm-specific summary</span></div>
    <div><span class="k">VBF H&rarr;cc / bb kept by the planned menu</span><span class="v">58% / 51%</span><span class="s">of events in a VBF + cc / bb acceptance; a tagged VBF seed at +2&nbsp;kHz: cc 61% (NN) &rarr; 62% (pixels), bb 56% &rarr; 61%</span></div>
    <div><span class="k">Boosted ggH (Higgs p<sub>T</sub> &gt; 200&nbsp;GeV) kept by the planned menu</span><span class="v">98&ndash;100%</span><span class="s">little L1 loss left; ZH(&nu;&nu;) with MET &gt; 150&nbsp;GeV: 96% (bb) / 98% (cc) of all such events</span></div>
  </div>
  <figure>{img("ctag_roc.png", "ROC curves for L1 charm tagging, c versus light and c versus b, for the L1 NN, Outer-Tracker-only displaced tracks, L1 tracks with pixel hits and HLT pixel tracks")}
    <figcaption><b>Pixels nearly double the L1 charm efficiency:</b> 16% &rarr; 29% at 10% light mistag.</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>c efficiency (QCD jets)</th><th class="n">vs light 1%</th><th class="n">vs light 10%</th><th class="n">vs b 30%</th><th class="n">Bits</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Today&#39;s L1 NN</td><td class="n">5.1%</td><td class="n">15.6%</td><td class="n">40.7%</td><td class="n">&mdash;</td></tr>
    <tr><td>+ pixel summary (8 numbers)</td><td class="n">6.7%</td><td class="n">29.0%</td><td class="n">61.1%</td><td class="n">64</td></tr>
    <tr><td>+ charm word on the same inputs</td><td class="n">7.0%</td><td class="n">29.0%</td><td class="n">62.3%</td><td class="n">+61</td></tr>
    <tr class="hl"><td><b>Recalibrated 3D impact parameter + charm word</b></td><td class="n"><b>10.4%</b></td><td class="n"><b>33.5%</b></td><td class="n"><b>66.2%</b></td><td class="n">125</td></tr>
